# Files excluded from the EAS build upload.
#
# IMPORTANT: when this file exists, EAS uses it INSTEAD of .gitignore — it does
# not merge the two. Everything that must stay out of the upload has to be
# listed here explicitly, including node_modules.

# --- Standard excludes (normally covered by .gitignore) ---
node_modules/
.git/
.expo/
.eas/
# …but keep the EAS Workflow definitions themselves.
!.eas/workflows/
android/
ios/
dist/
build/
coverage/
.DS_Store
*.log

# --- Local GitHub Packages auth ---
# Contains ${GITHUB_TOKEN}, which does not exist in the EAS build container, so
# yarn aborts before installing anything:
#   error Failed to replace env in config: ${GITHUB_TOKEN}
# No @marketingtool-pro package is an actual dependency.
.npmrc
**/.npmrc

# --- Competing lockfiles ---
# package-lock.json is deliberately NOT listed here. It is THE lockfile for this
# repo (npm; there is no yarn.lock and yarn was dropped — see .gitignore). This
# block used to exclude it, under a stale "EAS must resolve with yarn only"
# assumption, which meant every EAS build uploaded with no lockfile at all. EAS
# then re-resolved from the semver ranges in package.json, so pinned versions
# were not honoured on the builder: `@shopify/react-native-skia: "^2.6.5"`
# resolved to 2.11.0 there and broke the Android link with undefined
# facebook::jsi::* symbols. `expo-doctor` on the build also reported
# "No lock file detected". Keep the genuinely competing lockfiles out so npm is
# the one that resolves, and let package-lock.json through so builds are
# reproducible.
bun.lock
bun.lockb
pnpm-lock.yaml

# --- Vendored projects that are not part of the app ---
# These add gigabytes to the upload and drag unrelated Ruby/Maven/Go/Elixir
# manifests into dependency scanning.
m3/
jsonschex/
externals/
bundletool-1.18.3/
terraform-provider-exampletime/
circleci-runner/
travis-build/
gh-cli/
zsh-build/
conductor/
MyMacro/
my-env-plugin/
marketingtool/
AiMarketingtool-pro-fbaf2fa/
erl_crash.dump

# --- Backend packages: deployed separately, not bundled into the app ---
functions/
appwrite-functions/
infra/
src/api/

# --- Repo tooling and docs ---
.github/
docs/
fastlane/
# NOT scripts/ — package.json runs `node scripts/fix-gradle.js` as both
# eas-build-pre-install and eas-build-post-install. Excluding it made EAS
# upload an archive without the file, so the Pre-install hook phase failed
# with "Unknown error" before dependencies were even installed.
test/
Tests/
Sources/
plugin-rn-mcp/
profile-out/
build-logs.md
*.png.bak
